Given a number n, find all prime factors of n.Note :  Prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that has exactly two factors:1 and itself.Examples:Input: n = 18Output: [2, 3, 3]Explanation: The prime factorization of 18 is 2×32.Input: n = 25Output: [5, 5]Explanation: The prime factorization of  25 is 52.Try It YourselfTable of Content[Naive Approach] Iterative Time O(n) and space O(1) [Expected Approach] Prime Factorisation Time O(sqrt(n)) and Space (1) [Naive Approach] Iterative Time O(n) and space O(1)Step by Step implementation:Start a loop from i = 2 up to n.For each i, check if n is divisible by i (i.e n % i == 0).While n is divisible by i, store i as a factor and divide n by i.Continue this process for all i up to n to extract all prime factors.
            C++

    #include <iostream>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

vector<int> primeFactor (int n ){
    vector<int> ans ;
    for (int i = 2 ; i <= n ; i++){

        // n %  i  == 0 means n is divisible by i 
        while (n % i == 0 && n > 0 ){
            ans.push_back(i);
            n = n / i ;
        }
    }
    return ans ;
}
int main() {
    int n =  18;
    vector <int> ans = primeFactor(n);
    for (auto x : ans ){
        cout << x  <<' ';
    }
    return 0 ;
}


